{"id": "EUVD-2026-108316", "enisaUuid": "42937276-1136-3ea1-ae94-a9c4eef12410", "description": "Wasmtime before 36.0.16, 37.0.0 before 48.0.3, and 49.0.0 before 49.0.1 contains a denial of service vulnerability in wasmtime-wasi that allows guest WASI programs to panic the host via overflowing filesystem timestamps. Attackers can pass atim or mtim values whose sub-second field overflows the seconds field to path_filestat_set_times, fd_filestat_set_times, set-times, or set-times-at, crashing the host.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:53", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-j2g9-4prp-pf6h", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wasmtime-before-36.0.16-37.0.0-before-48.0.3-and-49.0.0-before-49.0.1-host-panic-via-wasi-filesystem-timestamp-overflow"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115387", "GHSA-xxx8-c5qx-wvm3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06b86d0b-30e5-39f2-b91a-05ea6737c6d8", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "0 <36.0.16"}, {"id": "44e40aba-505e-36d5-9ec3-d719ce995d3f", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "37.0.0 <48.0.3"}, {"id": "dc307a42-ef94-3a8b-9608-fcd305d5a3fb", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "49.0.0 <49.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "87282b52-7c45-3143-96ae-4795284cc64e", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}], "isExploited": false}